    "id": "f3_h3_quotient_anharmonic_antipodal_twin",
    "title": "H3 quotient anharmonic symmetry and antipodal twin",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "The quotient weight R(t) is constant on the six-value anharmonic orbit of every nonzero nonidentity target. On an antipodal target t=1-a^2, tau(t)=t/(t-1)=1-a^(-2) has exactly the same product richness P and quotient weight R. Antipodal P and M_a=P-2 are even, so P>=25 is exactly P>=26 and M_a>=24. This canonicalizes antipodal target evaluation but does not preserve or identify signed-disjoint edge counts.",
